WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.158 --> 00:00:02.115
- Drive is the mode where you're in charge

00:00:02.115 --> 00:00:03.532
of your thoughts.

00:00:08.273 --> 00:00:10.249
Whenever you start
feeling in your life like,

00:00:10.249 --> 00:00:14.416
oh my gosh, is this all there
is, huge red flag number one.

00:00:25.553 --> 00:00:26.472
How scared are you?

00:00:26.472 --> 00:00:27.692
- Less.

00:00:27.692 --> 00:00:30.906
- She'll be speaking at the
next conference, you watch.

00:00:30.906 --> 00:00:32.058
- Hello, Believe Nation.

00:00:32.058 --> 00:00:34.372
I'm Evan Carmichael,
my one word is Believe.

00:00:34.372 --> 00:00:36.554
And I believe that
entrepreneurs are going to solve

00:00:36.554 --> 00:00:39.189
all of the world's major problems

00:00:39.189 --> 00:00:40.224
So to help you on your journey today,

00:00:40.224 --> 00:00:43.105
we're going to learn from
TV host, author and speaker

00:00:43.105 --> 00:00:46.461
Mel Robbins and my take on
her Top 10 Rules of Success,

00:00:46.461 --> 00:00:47.524
Volume 2.

00:00:47.524 --> 00:00:49.277
Rule number one is my personal favorite.

00:00:49.277 --> 00:00:51.365
I'd love to know which one
you guys like the best.

00:00:51.365 --> 00:00:53.020
And as always, as you're listening,

00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:54.698
if something really resonates with you,

00:00:54.698 --> 00:00:56.857
there's a message that
really holds true to you,

00:00:56.857 --> 00:00:58.774
please leave it down in the Comments below

00:00:58.774 --> 00:01:01.704
and put it in quotes so that
other people can be inspired

00:01:01.704 --> 00:01:04.247
and when you write it down,
it's much more likely to stick

00:01:04.247 --> 00:01:06.168
with yourself as well.

00:01:06.168 --> 00:01:07.076
Enjoy!

00:01:07.076 --> 00:01:09.159
(whoosh)

00:01:20.218 --> 00:01:22.234
- Drive, that's this puppy right here.

00:01:22.234 --> 00:01:24.906
This is what you want, this
is your prefrontal cortex.

00:01:24.906 --> 00:01:28.991
Drive is the mode where you're
in charge of your thoughts.

00:01:28.991 --> 00:01:33.321
It's where you are fully
awake, you are present

00:01:33.321 --> 00:01:36.244
and you are driving your
thoughts and actions.

00:01:36.244 --> 00:01:39.486
When you're doing that,
your prefrontal cortex

00:01:39.486 --> 00:01:40.984
is active.

00:01:40.984 --> 00:01:43.600
The prefrontal cortex is the
part of the brain that you need

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:45.910
in order to learn new behavior,

00:01:45.910 --> 00:01:47.856
in order to do something difficult,

00:01:47.856 --> 00:01:49.642
in order to do something uncertain,

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:51.649
in order to do strategic thinking.

00:01:51.649 --> 00:01:53.278
I'm going to give you an example.

00:01:53.278 --> 00:01:54.752
So I'm a rightie.

00:01:54.752 --> 00:01:56.639
If I were to try to
write with my left hand,

00:01:56.639 --> 00:01:57.472
and like you,

00:01:57.472 --> 00:01:59.076
Lewis is going to torture me--
- Sure.

00:01:59.076 --> 00:02:01.253
and tie my hand behind my
back and make me like do this,

00:02:01.253 --> 00:02:02.498
I could do it.

00:02:02.498 --> 00:02:04.549
It would look like I was
writing with my foot.

00:02:04.549 --> 00:02:05.430
(laughs)

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:07.100
And if Lewis came up to me and said,

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:08.466
hey Mel, you want some BulletProof Coffee?

00:02:08.466 --> 00:02:10.689
I'd be like, Lewis I'm
trying to concentrate.

00:02:10.689 --> 00:02:11.901
I can't do this.

00:02:11.901 --> 00:02:15.275
My prefrontal cortex would be el fuego

00:02:15.275 --> 00:02:19.009
because it is firing on all cylinders

00:02:19.009 --> 00:02:22.991
to communicate to my hand, new behavior.

00:02:22.991 --> 00:02:26.012
So, the thing that's cool about that

00:02:26.012 --> 00:02:28.929
is that you can use a simple trick.

00:02:30.026 --> 00:02:31.943
The moment you feel yourself hesitate,

00:02:31.943 --> 00:02:33.518
the moment you've got one of those moments

00:02:33.518 --> 00:02:34.726
where you know that you need to,

00:02:34.726 --> 00:02:36.254
this is that moment that
Lewis talks to you about

00:02:36.254 --> 00:02:37.998
where you got to step
outside of your comfort zone

00:02:37.998 --> 00:02:39.792
and you got to lean into your passion.

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:41.768
And you've got to really take some risks.

00:02:41.768 --> 00:02:44.239
And you got to feel the fear
and you got to do it anyway.

00:02:44.239 --> 00:02:46.883
That's the moment where you just woke up.

00:02:46.883 --> 00:02:48.638
Now you got a decision to make.

00:02:48.638 --> 00:02:50.349
Are you going to drift
back into the habits

00:02:50.349 --> 00:02:52.882
or are you going to awaken
your prefrontal cortex

00:02:52.882 --> 00:02:53.975
and drive forward and focus

00:02:53.975 --> 00:02:55.725
and do something new?

00:08:23.017 --> 00:08:25.780
I want you to start
seeing something bigger.

00:08:25.780 --> 00:08:27.208
I know you're all successful.

00:08:27.208 --> 00:08:30.399
I'm talking about something
really big for your life.

00:08:30.399 --> 00:08:34.566
And in order to do that, you
have to answer this question,

00:08:35.974 --> 00:08:38.490
what do you really want?

00:08:38.490 --> 00:08:41.225
Now I'm not talking about something small.

00:08:41.225 --> 00:08:44.021
I'm not talking about a little haiku.

00:08:44.021 --> 00:08:45.901
I'm not talking about
renovating your kitchen.

00:08:45.901 --> 00:08:48.995
I'm not talking about
signing on 10 new customers

00:08:48.995 --> 00:08:50.053
this month.

00:08:50.053 --> 00:08:53.303
I'm talking about what you really want.

00:08:55.286 --> 00:08:58.558
You know three years ago, I was a lawyer

00:08:58.558 --> 00:09:01.779
and a business coach
working with private clients

00:09:01.779 --> 00:09:04.417
and big corporations all over the country.

00:09:04.417 --> 00:09:07.855
And I came to a seminar,
just like this one.

00:09:07.855 --> 00:09:10.314
A big leadership seminar and
I went there with my husband,

00:09:10.314 --> 00:09:11.773
we're both business owners.

00:09:11.773 --> 00:09:14.489
I went because I wanted
to be more successful.

00:09:14.489 --> 00:09:17.803
I went because I wanted
to make even more money

00:09:17.803 --> 00:09:18.897
than I already did.

00:09:18.897 --> 00:09:20.966
I was sitting exactly
where you are, in fact,

00:09:20.966 --> 00:09:23.476
I was sitting about, I
don't know, 15 rows back

00:09:23.476 --> 00:09:26.474
right where that woman with
her hand on, her hand, yet you.

00:09:26.474 --> 00:09:27.992
Yeah, she's like, hi!

00:09:27.992 --> 00:09:29.912
I was sitting and I was taking notes

00:09:29.912 --> 00:09:32.488
and I'm like, okay I'm
sure to make more money.

00:09:32.488 --> 00:09:36.487
And then all of a sudden,
she walked on the stage.

00:09:36.487 --> 00:09:38.154
That is Martha Beck.

00:09:39.690 --> 00:09:42.473
She writes a column for Oprah Winfrey.

00:09:42.473 --> 00:09:45.218
She travels around the country speaking.

00:09:45.218 --> 00:09:47.087
She's a best-selling author.

00:09:47.087 --> 00:09:51.254
And when she walked on-stage,
I literally stopped listening.

00:09:53.243 --> 00:09:54.878
Please keep listening to me, right now.

00:09:54.878 --> 00:09:56.536
(audience laughs)

00:09:56.536 --> 00:09:57.703
And it hit me.

00:09:59.017 --> 00:10:01.517
I said, I want to be doing that.

00:10:02.762 --> 00:10:05.992
I'm ready for a bigger
state, like that's it.

00:10:05.992 --> 00:10:07.288
And what's so interesting

00:10:07.288 --> 00:10:09.150
about when you answer that question

00:10:09.150 --> 00:10:13.492
is that you don't answer it
up here, you answer it here.

00:10:13.492 --> 00:10:16.489
That's how you see something
bigger for yourself.

00:10:16.489 --> 00:10:18.541
You guy are really cute
because everybody's like,

00:10:18.541 --> 00:10:19.439
I don't see it.

00:10:19.439 --> 00:10:21.704
I don't see anything for myself right now.

00:10:21.704 --> 00:10:24.683
Now I'm just confused, I
thought I knew what I wanted.

00:10:24.683 --> 00:10:28.266
And you know, now Mel,
I'm not really sure.

00:10:29.226 --> 00:10:31.976
Right now, the economy is so bad.

00:10:32.836 --> 00:10:36.345
I mean, it's so bad that
even if you're successful.

00:10:36.345 --> 00:10:39.042
I know sometimes I feel embarrassed
talking about my success

00:10:39.042 --> 00:10:41.033
around some of my friends because I know

00:10:41.033 --> 00:10:43.155
that they're really struggling.

00:10:43.155 --> 00:10:46.328
I get calls everyday into the radio show.

00:10:46.328 --> 00:10:49.093
People saying, oh I've got this great idea

00:10:49.093 --> 00:10:52.619
but I just don't know
if it's the right time.

00:10:52.619 --> 00:10:53.765
You know what I say to them?

00:10:53.765 --> 00:10:56.491
I say, yeah you know, you're right.

00:10:56.491 --> 00:10:58.074
The recession, it's huge.

00:10:58.074 --> 00:10:58.907
You should wait.

00:10:58.907 --> 00:11:00.820
Those dreams yeah, put 'em on hold.

00:11:00.820 --> 00:11:01.723
That's right.

00:11:01.723 --> 00:11:04.064
You should stay in that
job you can't stand

00:11:04.064 --> 00:11:05.557
just a little bit longer.

00:11:05.557 --> 00:11:07.457
You got college bills to pay.

00:11:07.457 --> 00:11:09.288
I mean, what you're doing it's fine.

00:11:09.288 --> 00:11:11.653
You're busy, right?

00:11:11.653 --> 00:11:14.322
That guy you're dating,
he's good enough for you

00:11:14.322 --> 00:11:17.739
but for the people in this room, baloney.

00:11:18.575 --> 00:11:19.887
You know, that's right.

00:11:19.887 --> 00:11:23.301
You know exactly what you want.

00:11:23.301 --> 00:11:28.262
And the only thing that you
need to do is to admit it.

00:11:28.262 --> 00:11:29.822
Now this may sound weird
because I know most of you

00:11:29.822 --> 00:11:30.988
came in here because you're like,

00:11:30.988 --> 00:11:32.430
I know what I want, I'm here with success

00:11:32.430 --> 00:11:33.626
to try to figure it out.

00:11:33.626 --> 00:11:36.543
I'm talking about something bigger.

00:11:37.688 --> 00:11:38.688
Much bigger.

00:11:41.044 --> 00:11:44.984
I'll admit to you what
it is that I'm up to.

00:11:44.984 --> 00:11:47.917
And the truth is, it's embarrassing

00:11:47.917 --> 00:11:51.035
because when you lock
onto something way bigger

00:11:51.035 --> 00:11:54.602
than where you're at, it
is downright embarrassing

00:11:54.602 --> 00:11:55.826
to tell people

00:11:55.826 --> 00:11:58.400
because you're not there yet.

00:11:58.400 --> 00:11:59.496
But I mean, at this rate,

00:11:59.496 --> 00:12:01.554
I've already admitted to you
that I stalked Martha Beck

00:12:01.554 --> 00:12:04.267
and that I brought a haiku
to the best Lit agent

00:12:04.267 --> 00:12:07.428
in the country so I got
nothing to lose at this point.

00:12:07.428 --> 00:12:09.345
So this is what I want.

00:12:12.534 --> 00:12:14.013
(audience laughs)

00:12:14.013 --> 00:12:16.910
Well not him, I'm married.

00:12:16.910 --> 00:12:19.019
I want what he's got.

00:12:19.019 --> 00:12:21.186
I want 600 radio stations.

00:12:22.229 --> 00:12:25.069
I want two million listeners.

00:12:25.069 --> 00:12:27.860
And I could certainly deal
with the $400 million salary.

00:12:27.860 --> 00:12:30.247
In fact, if I got it, I'd
renovate everybody's kitchen.

00:12:30.247 --> 00:12:31.723
(audience laughs)

00:12:31.723 --> 00:12:34.631
And you know, the thing is
though what's so interesting

00:12:34.631 --> 00:12:38.274
about this is that I didn't pick him.

00:12:38.274 --> 00:12:41.606
I mean, I'm not looking
to become a cigar-smoking,

00:12:41.606 --> 00:12:45.242
Conservative political guy
that like stirs the pot

00:12:45.242 --> 00:12:47.307
and makes everybody all mad.

00:12:47.307 --> 00:12:49.227
I'm the liberal lifestyle gal

00:12:49.227 --> 00:12:51.111
that's trying to help people out.

00:12:51.111 --> 00:12:54.877
But what I want to do
is I want to use radio

00:12:54.877 --> 00:12:59.695
to entertain people and help
them achieve their dreams.

00:12:59.695 --> 00:13:02.287
And when I really think about it,

00:13:02.287 --> 00:13:05.311
he's the one that's in the front.

00:13:05.311 --> 00:13:08.858
I want to not only reach what's
he doing, I want to surpass him.

00:13:08.858 --> 00:13:10.271
I mean, do you think I like it

00:13:10.271 --> 00:13:12.738
when my friends come over
to my office in Boston

00:13:12.738 --> 00:13:15.352
at my house and they're
like, what is that guy doing

00:13:15.352 --> 00:13:16.594
on your board?

00:13:16.594 --> 00:13:19.165
(audience laughs)

00:13:19.165 --> 00:13:21.807
No, it's embarrassing.

00:13:21.807 --> 00:13:24.995
When you admit the big
thing that you're up to,

00:13:24.995 --> 00:13:26.270
it's embarrassing.

00:13:26.270 --> 00:13:29.568
I have 40 stations, he's got 600.

00:13:29.568 --> 00:13:34.096
There's a big gap so admitting
where you want to get to

00:13:34.096 --> 00:13:35.346
is embarrassing

00:13:36.447 --> 00:13:37.588
but you got to do it.

00:13:37.588 --> 00:13:39.784
- Mel Robbins, your radio
show, Make It Happen,

00:13:39.784 --> 00:13:41.001
helps people go for success.

00:13:41.001 --> 00:13:43.690
You actually say there are three red flags

00:13:43.690 --> 00:13:45.370
we should look for that
will actually tell us

00:13:45.370 --> 00:13:46.739
it's time to change.

00:13:46.739 --> 00:13:47.572
- Big ones.

00:13:47.572 --> 00:13:49.551
Whenever you start
feeling in your life like,

00:13:49.551 --> 00:13:53.009
oh my gosh, is this all there is?

00:13:53.009 --> 00:13:54.464
Huge red flag number one.

00:13:54.464 --> 00:13:57.247
Number two, when you spend
your energy being jealous

00:13:57.247 --> 00:13:59.632
or having the grass is greener over there,

00:13:59.632 --> 00:14:01.431
another big wake-up call for you

00:14:01.431 --> 00:14:02.741
that you're ready for a change.

00:14:02.741 --> 00:14:05.049
And then the other final red flag is

00:14:05.049 --> 00:14:07.624
if you're spending your
life waiting to be happy.

00:14:07.624 --> 00:14:08.826
I'll be happy when,

00:14:08.826 --> 00:14:10.021
I'll be happy when I get married.

00:14:10.021 --> 00:14:11.267
I'll be happy when I change my job.

00:14:11.267 --> 00:14:13.260
I'll be happy when I want your business.

00:14:13.260 --> 00:14:16.369
It's time to change now 'cause
that moment's not coming

00:14:16.369 --> 00:14:17.749
unless you make it come.

00:14:17.749 --> 00:14:20.460
- But how do I know that
I'm maybe not just living in

00:14:20.460 --> 00:14:21.643
a fantasy land, that I'm never going to,

00:14:21.643 --> 00:14:24.141
no matter where I am, the
grass is always greener concept

00:14:24.141 --> 00:14:26.005
that oh we say, this could be better

00:14:26.005 --> 00:14:27.787
and then I might be making
change for change sake

00:14:27.787 --> 00:14:29.233
but it might not be really what I need.

00:14:29.233 --> 00:14:31.629
- Baloney, if you're still
saying that to yourself

00:14:31.629 --> 00:14:32.913
over and over and over again

00:14:32.913 --> 00:14:35.237
and you're complaining,
what you're really good at

00:14:35.237 --> 00:14:36.952
is ignoring your gut.

00:14:36.952 --> 00:14:38.885
So it's time to start tuning into your gut

00:14:38.885 --> 00:14:40.002
and making some changes.

00:14:40.002 --> 00:14:41.167
- Okay so people see these signs,

00:14:41.167 --> 00:14:42.355
why don't they make changes then?

00:14:42.355 --> 00:14:43.704
I mean what you just
described is very depressing.

00:14:43.704 --> 00:14:45.182
- I can tell you why, I can tell you why.

00:14:45.182 --> 00:14:46.341
The reason why they don't make changes

00:14:46.341 --> 00:14:48.389
is because what happens is, you say,

00:14:48.389 --> 00:14:51.524
okay I want to do X and then
immediately what you see next

00:14:51.524 --> 00:14:53.483
are all the obstacles.

00:14:53.483 --> 00:14:56.178
And so you're actually smart,
you're not necessarily afraid.

00:14:56.178 --> 00:14:57.988
You're smart because you think,
how the hell am I going to go

00:14:57.988 --> 00:15:00.619
from being a lawyer to a carpenter

00:15:00.619 --> 00:15:02.147
when I have a mortgage to pay.

00:15:02.147 --> 00:15:03.477
I've got tuition bills to go.

00:15:03.477 --> 00:15:05.500
My wife is going to kill me
if I make this kind of change.

00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:08.568
So you get stuck because you see obstacles

00:15:08.568 --> 00:15:09.692
and then you never do anything.

00:15:09.692 --> 00:15:10.528
- Those are very real obstacles.

00:15:10.528 --> 00:15:11.519
- Of course they are.
- Okay so--

00:15:11.519 --> 00:15:13.136
how do I kind of get past those obstacles?

00:15:13.136 --> 00:15:15.392
Very easy, let's say I
recognize the warning signals.

00:15:15.392 --> 00:15:16.484
Okay, time for change.

00:15:16.484 --> 00:15:17.862
Danger, Will Robinson.

00:15:17.862 --> 00:15:21.569
This is not the right path
but it does seem Herculean

00:15:21.569 --> 00:15:22.888
the hurdles I have to go over.

00:15:22.888 --> 00:15:25.427
- Don't quit your job, that's number one.

00:15:25.427 --> 00:15:27.812
Second thing is, I think
most change in life

00:15:27.812 --> 00:15:31.704
is not about putting on a big
cape and jumping off a cliff,

00:15:31.704 --> 00:15:32.636
or out of an airplane.

00:15:32.636 --> 00:15:34.510
It's more like leaning into something.

00:15:34.510 --> 00:15:36.957
So if you find yourself
daydreaming about something

00:15:36.957 --> 00:15:38.902
or wishing that you
could change your life,

00:15:38.902 --> 00:15:40.497
start investigating.

00:15:40.497 --> 00:15:42.017
Start having conversations about it.

00:15:42.017 --> 00:15:44.184
Start leaning into change.

00:24:05.189 --> 00:24:06.592
If you took money off the table,

00:24:06.592 --> 00:24:07.811
if you didn't give a (speech muted)

00:24:07.811 --> 00:24:08.955
what anybody else thought,

00:24:08.955 --> 00:24:11.038
what's the thing you
would love to be doing

00:24:11.038 --> 00:24:12.991
with your life, seriously?

00:24:12.991 --> 00:24:15.354
Do you dream of being a
professional photographer?

00:24:15.354 --> 00:24:17.027
Do you want to open your own restaurant?

00:24:17.027 --> 00:24:19.203
You always thought about
traveling the world

00:24:19.203 --> 00:24:22.457
and entertaining kids
with your juggling skills.

00:24:22.457 --> 00:24:24.690
I don't know, it's your life.

00:24:24.690 --> 00:24:26.804
You get to choose what you want to do.

00:24:26.804 --> 00:24:28.675
Be honest with yourself.

00:24:28.675 --> 00:24:31.850
What is it that you would
want to do with your life

00:24:31.850 --> 00:24:35.158
if you didn't have to
pay the bills doing it.

00:24:35.158 --> 00:24:36.571
Another thing you can ask yourself,

00:24:36.571 --> 00:24:38.454
who do you find yourself
sort of envious of?

00:24:38.454 --> 00:24:40.754
You know like you look at
their life and you just think,

00:24:40.754 --> 00:24:43.497
gosh, how awesome that
they get to do that.

00:24:43.497 --> 00:24:47.064
Well, once you have that
answer for yourself,

00:24:47.064 --> 00:24:48.469
you've gotten really honest.

00:24:48.469 --> 00:24:49.732
You pushed the bull (speech muted) aside

00:24:49.732 --> 00:24:51.781
and you really asked it for yourself

00:24:51.781 --> 00:24:53.984
and answered the question honestly,

00:24:53.984 --> 00:24:55.922
all you got to do is
explore it, that's it.

00:24:55.922 --> 00:24:58.987
Just find one thing that you can do

00:24:58.987 --> 00:25:02.423
to enrich and expand
your knowledge about it.

00:25:02.423 --> 00:25:05.145
Find one course online, Google the topic.

00:25:05.145 --> 00:25:08.378
Stalk people that are
pursuing this line of work.

00:25:08.378 --> 00:25:11.486
That's how you start to do it.

00:25:11.486 --> 00:25:13.220
One step at a time.

00:25:13.220 --> 00:25:14.981
So start with answering the question,

00:25:14.981 --> 00:25:18.243
what do you really want, with
a massive dose of honesty.

00:25:18.243 --> 00:25:21.489
Google the topic and find
one thing that you can do,

00:25:21.489 --> 00:25:22.322
just one.

00:25:22.322 --> 00:25:25.028
Push yourself and start to explore.

00:25:25.028 --> 00:25:27.762
If you were to wake up and
do that every single day,

00:25:27.762 --> 00:25:31.730
spend 10 minutes a day,
you would be startled,

00:25:31.730 --> 00:25:34.238
astonished by what your
life looks like in a matter

00:25:34.238 --> 00:25:35.886
of a year or two.

00:25:35.886 --> 00:25:38.902
What is the biggest obstacle that we face?

00:25:38.902 --> 00:25:40.709
Tiago, it's simple.

00:25:40.709 --> 00:25:41.964
It's self-doubt.

00:25:41.964 --> 00:25:45.026
It's not fear, it's not lack of money.

00:25:45.026 --> 00:25:46.918
It's not lack of supporters.

00:25:46.918 --> 00:25:49.712
It's the fact that deep down inside,

00:25:49.712 --> 00:25:54.087
you will doubt yourself
at critical moments.

00:25:54.087 --> 00:25:56.614
And here's the problem with self-doubt.

00:25:56.614 --> 00:25:59.267
Self-doubt doesn't have to stop you.

00:25:59.267 --> 00:26:03.227
The problem with self-doubt
is that the second that you

00:26:03.227 --> 00:26:06.729
feel a little doubtful,
the second that you start

00:26:06.729 --> 00:26:10.989
to question yourself,
you physically hesitate.

00:26:10.989 --> 00:26:15.072
That hesitation has become
a habit that stops you

00:26:15.984 --> 00:26:19.251
because the moment you hesitate,
it wakes up your brain.

00:26:19.251 --> 00:26:22.270
Your brain starts thinking and
then you hold yourself back.

00:26:22.270 --> 00:26:25.615
You guys know I talk about
the 5-Second Rule incessantly.

00:26:25.615 --> 00:26:27.296
It's the title of the
new book that I'm writing

00:26:27.296 --> 00:26:29.852
that's coming out in 2017.

00:26:29.852 --> 00:26:34.724
The 5-Second Rule is a tool
that battles self-doubt

00:26:34.724 --> 00:26:39.156
because in those moments,
those tiny micro-moments,

00:26:39.156 --> 00:26:42.006
when you're faced with, should
I do this or should I not?

00:26:42.006 --> 00:26:43.481
Should I speak in a meeting?

00:26:43.481 --> 00:26:45.320
Should I hold back my ideas?

00:26:45.320 --> 00:26:47.162
Should I have this tough conversation?

00:26:47.162 --> 00:26:49.489
Or should I wait 'til later?

00:26:49.489 --> 00:26:53.993
The second you doubt the
option of moving forward,

00:26:53.993 --> 00:26:55.076
you hesitate.

00:26:55.917 --> 00:26:58.434
Then you think, then you hold back.

00:26:58.434 --> 00:27:01.826
That's how it happens every single time.

00:27:01.826 --> 00:27:03.606
That's how you sabotage your success.

00:27:03.606 --> 00:27:06.248
That's how you rob yourself of joy.

00:27:06.248 --> 00:27:08.331
That habit of hesitating,

00:27:09.454 --> 00:27:11.840
the moment that you feel doubt

00:27:11.840 --> 00:27:14.414
is killing your dreams.

00:27:14.414 --> 00:27:17.967
The single biggest obstacle in life, Tiago

00:27:17.967 --> 00:27:20.614
is the doubt that you feel.

00:27:20.614 --> 00:27:24.516
And the single biggest
mistake that you're making

00:27:24.516 --> 00:27:28.200
is that you hesitate when you feel it.

00:27:28.200 --> 00:27:30.744
If you start to use the
5-Second Rule in those moments

00:27:30.744 --> 00:27:34.583
to just physically move
forward within five seconds,

00:27:34.583 --> 00:27:37.166
feeling that doubt, you'll win.

